# linkedin's read quota and the day's budgets (core/modules/linkedin/README.md "API"): an account's
# reads today over its cap, its limits today and its working-hours window. One variable besides the
# usual ones goes in http-client.private.env.json: `accountId`, an id GET …/linkedin/accounts answers.

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/linkedin/accounts/{id}/usage: the account's reads today, reserved and made, over its cap, and whether its window is open; beside them readAllowance, invites { used, limit }, messages { used, limit }, withdrawals { used, max }, weekInvites { used, cap } and actions { used, max }, used being reserved plus made (beta-p1-020)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/linkedin/accounts/{{accountId}}/usage
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
